  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe rest group of the 2D Pocket has a new mode, \"previous operations\".\nIn this mode the rest area is read from the stock that the earlier operations of the same setup leave.\nThe entered-tool mode of #1489 does not change, and it stays the default.\n\n- `RestParams` has the field `source` (`RestSource::EnteredTool` or `RestSource::PreviousOperations`).\n- `machining2d::rest_pocket_previous` plans the rest passes from a column grid.\n  `rest_stock_from_columns` builds the `RestStock` of #2031 from that grid, one floor for each cut depth.\n  `rest_plan_stock` makes the rest area from it.\n- The grid is the one that `rest::prior_state` builds for the 3D Pocket: the setup stock, cut by the cached paths of the earlier operations, each with its tool shape.\n- The reading is conservative:\n  - A column stands at a cut depth when its top is above that depth. A floor allowance is material.\n  - The standing columns grow by one cell diagonal.\n  - A column that cannot be read stands. The pocket outside the grid stands.\n  - The rest area is the union over all cut depths. A roughing pass that stops above the floor leaves the whole pocket.\n- The two modes never use the planner of the other mode. Each planner refuses the other mode by name.\n- The mode rides the existing `EditOperationParams` command (undo and redo), the project key `rest.source` and the MCP `edit_operation` parameter.\n  A file without the key reads as the entered tool.\n- The Pocket page has the row \"Rest stock from\". The previous tool rows hide in the new mode.\n\nGeneration refuses by name when the stock cannot be established:\n\n- an earlier operation of the setup has no toolpath;\n- an earlier operation of the setup has a stale toolpath;\n- an earlier operation of the setup is suppressed and has a cut on record;\n- the Pocket is tilted (also refused at the edit).\n\nWhen no earlier operation cut, the stock is known. The whole pocket is cut and a note says it.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe rest generator trusted the entered previous tool.\nIt could not see the depth that the earlier operation reached (#1490, item 3).\n\n## Tests\n\nPins, all new:\n\n- `crates/motion/src/machining2d/rest_prior_tests.rs` (lib): `each_reading_guard_is_pinned_and_its_removal_fails_the_pin`, `a_floor_cut_at_the_cut_depth_does_not_stand_and_one_above_it_does`, `bad_input_is_refused_by_name`.\n- `crates/motion/tests/rest_previous.rs`: 6 tests. They compare the rest area with an independent simulation of the earlier operations: a flat tool, a wall allowance, a bull-nose tool, mixed tools with a partial depth and disconnected cuts, an island. The rest path cuts each column that was left and cuts no wall.\n- `crates/app/tests/rest_previous_ops.rs`: 7 tests. The real job against an independent simulation; the shallow roughing pass; the four refusals; stale after a changed tool, depth and order; `RegenerateAll`; undo and redo; the project file; MCP with save and reopen.\n- `crates/app/src/operation/rest_op_tests.rs`: `the_rest_group_moves_the_stamp` now also covers the mode.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/rest_source_tests.rs`: 2 tests for the new row.\n\nRed before the change: the pins use the new API and do not compile on `upstream/main`. Thus the mutation results below are the proof for each guard.\n\nMutations (one guard removed, its pin run, then restored):\n\n| Guard removed | Pin | Mutant | Restored |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| every cut depth is read (`Guards::depth`) | `each_reading_guard_...` | red | green |\n| an unreadable column stands (`Guards::unknown`) | `each_reading_guard_...` | red | green |\n| the pocket outside the grid stands (`Guards::outside`) | `each_reading_guard_...` | red | green |\n| one cell of growth (`Guards::cell`) | `each_reading_guard_...` | red | green |\n| `rest_plan` refuses the new mode | `the_two_rest_modes_never_use_each_others_planner` | red | green |\n| `rest_pocket_previous` refuses the entered mode | same | red | green |\n| `validate` does not read the previous tool in the new mode | same | red | green |\n| job: tilted plane refused | `a_tilted_plane_is_refused_by_name_at_the_edit_and_at_generation` | red | green |\n| door: tilted plane refused at the edit | same | red | green |\n| job: `previous_ops_refusal` is called | `a_stock_that_cannot_be_established_is_refused_by_name` | red | green |\n| earlier operation suppressed | same | red | green |\n| earlier operation stale | same | red | green |\n| earlier operation never generated | same | red | green |\n| the Pocket arm routes the mode | `the_rest_pass_cuts_what_the_simulated_roughing_pass_left` | red | green |\n| stamp byte 0xD8 | `the_rest_group_moves_the_stamp` | red | green |\n\nThe first four guards have a switch in the code (`rest_prior::Guards`), and the unit test turns each off. The other eleven were removed by hand.\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on the head merged with `upstream/main` c4ac3ce6d: green, 357 steps, 0 failed (29.2 min). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. `git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\" \"*.png\"` is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A setup whose stock is carried from an earlier setup (#318). The code path is `rest::prior_state`, which the 3D Pocket uses. No test here crosses a setup boundary. The check for stale operations reads the same setup only.\n- A WCS yaw. The existing `wcs_yaw::enter` turns the grid. No test here has a yaw.\n- The field stock engine (#586, #637). The reader is `Columns`, which reads the two engines. The tests use the column grid.\n- Zigzag and Offset rings in the new mode. They use the passes of the entered-tool mode, which has its own tests. The new tests use Waterline.\n- The pixel snapshots (release lane). The new row moves the rows of a Pocket page that has rest machining on.\n- The app was not started by hand. The UI tests ran the page in the test harness.\n\n## Known limits (recorded in `docs/decisions/2033-rest-previous-ops.md`)\n\n- One rest area for all levels. An upper level can cut air where only a lower level has material.\n- The strict reading keeps a band of about 1.5 cells along each wall that an earlier tool rode. The rest pass follows those walls.\n- The Adaptive strategy stays refused. The Adaptive strategy of the 2D Pocket is retired, so `rest_adaptive` has no door from this operation.\n- The MCP skill text (`.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md`) does not describe the new `source` key. The session could not write that file. That edit is owed.\n- The guide pages on the site do not describe the new mode.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #2716 changes `generate.rs`, `job.rs` and `params.rs` in other arms (the Contour kind). Different function parts. The PR that merges second refreshes.\n- #2714 changes `generate.rs`, `params.rs` and `machining2d/mod.rs` for the Slot Undercut kind. Different lines. The PR that merges second refreshes.\n- #2678 changes `generate.rs`, `job.rs` and `machining2d/mod.rs`. Its hunks are not in the rest branch of the Pocket arm. The PR that merges second refreshes.\n\nChangelog: The 2D Pocket's rest machining can read the remaining material from the previous operations of the setup (\"Rest stock from: Previous operations\"), at every cut depth, in place of an entered previous tool.\n\nEffort: max\n\nFixes #2033\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
